    "title": "Abdominal pain: possible TDF toxicity",
    "message": "Guidelines list abdominal pain or discomfort as a presenting sign of TDF toxicity including lactic acidosis or severe hepatomegaly with steatosis, and recommend doing LFTs and RFTs; if deranged, substitute TDF with ABC. Patient is on TDF and reports abdominal pain today. Appetite is preserved and no fever, which argues against severe toxicity or infection. However, no LFTs or RFTs have been ordered in the clinician's plan to evaluate this symptom. Creatinine was normal (82 umol/L) 78 days ago but does not rule out acute hepatotoxicity.",
